'   why this shape, measured ............ _spec/_experiments/mobile-device-reach.puml
'   the pattern it copies ............... _spec/internal/sbx/host-browser-cdp.puml
'   why the box has no emulator ......... _spec/_experiments/nested-sbx-kvm.puml
'
' ── WHY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The box has no /dev/kvm, so the emulator lives on the host. The host adb
' server is the one seam a fresh VM can use without the host's adbkey: the
' emulator's adbd refuses a fresh key, the server already holds the host's.
' The driver is mobile-next/mobile-mcp. Its tools are primitives (tap, swipe,
' type, element list, screenshot) and it runs no model, so the harness's own
' inference does the reasoning and the run needs no second provider or key.
'
' ── capabilities.hostDevices SELECTS THE ROWS ──────────────────────────────
'   android → addonAndroid  live under sbx; greyed without it
'   ios     → addonIOS      always greyed: "coming soon" (not built; iOS
'                           Simulators also need a macOS host with Xcode)
' `--addon android` resolves; `--addon ios` is refused with the same reason.
'
' ── HOST SIDE (internal/hostadb) ───────────────────────────────────────────
'   port    PROVEO_HOST_ADB_PORT, default 5037.
'   reuse   any serial the server lists in state "device" is reused as is.
'   launch  else `adb -P <port> start-server`, then `emulator -avd <avd>`
'           windowed, own process group, ANDROID_ADB_SERVER_PORT=<port>,
'           left open after the run. Wait: host:devices + sys.boot_completed=1.
'   avd     PROVEO_HOST_AVD when it names an AVD, else the first listed.
'   sdk     ANDROID_HOME > ANDROID_SDK_ROOT > ~/Library/Android/sdk (darwin)
'           > ~/Android/Sdk; each tool falls back to PATH.
'   kit     allow += localhost:<port>, registry.npmjs.org (the install).
'   env     PROVEO_HOST_ADB_PORT=<port>
'           ADB_SERVER_SOCKET=tcp:host.docker.internal:<port> — every process
'           in the sandbox (the agent's Bash, `--shell`) reaches the server;
'           adb resolves the name itself and ignores Host, unlike Chrome.
'   host os PROVEO_HOST_OS=<runtime.GOOS> into every sandbox (EnvHostOS),
'           for fixes measured on one host OS only.
'
' ── ONE ROW PER HARNESS (hostadb.Launches) ─────────────────────────────────
' A harness gets android only with a per-launch way to take the mobile server;
' a contract test fails a manifest that declares android without one, and an
' sbx harness with no row at all.
'   claudecode  --mcp-config <hostadb.MCPConfig>, prepended host-side by
'               withMobileMCP (sbx runs claude as its own agent, so the
'               image's entrypoint never launches it), as --chrome is
'   opencode    "mcp": {"mobile": {"type": "local", ...}} merged into the
'               OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT launchConfigEnv already builds
'   codex       not wired yet: -c mcp_servers.mobile.* per launch
'   cecli       not wired yet: --mcp-servers / CECLI_MCP_SERVERS
'   cursor      none: MCP only from a persistent ~/.cursor/mcp.json
'   hermes      none: MCP only from its persistent config.yaml; no built-in
'               Android control (the community plugin wants a local SDK)
'
' ── GUEST SIDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   image (base)               apt `adb` (Ubuntu 1:34.0.5): protocol 1.0.41,
'                              same as the host's 36.0.2, so the client never
'                              kills the host server over a version mismatch
'   proveo_host_adb_env        ADB_HOST/ADB_PORT from ADB_SERVER_SOCKET, else
'                              the resolved gateway IP + PROVEO_HOST_ADB_PORT
'   proveo_adb_mirror_start    `proveo-entrypoint adb-mirror` in the background
'   proveo_mobile_mcp_exec     the MCP server's command (bash -c, via the
'                              lib): env, mirror, npm-install
'                              @mobilenext/mobile-mcp at
'                              PROVEO_MOBILE_MCP_VERSION (1.0.6) into the
'                              toolchain home on first use, then exec it with
'                              MOBILEMCP_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1; stdout stays the
'                              server's alone, every notice goes to stderr
'
' ── WHY THE MIRROR (internal/adbmirror) ────────────────────────────────────
' mobilecli, mobile-mcp's driver, starts an on-device server and reaches it
' with `adb forward tcp:<P> localabstract:mobilecli-server`, then dials
' http://localhost:<P>. Behind a remote server that listener opens on the
' HOST's loopback, so element and tap calls read "device server did not
' start". mobilecli picks P free in the VM on purpose, for "tooling that
' tunnels forwarded ports by their number". The mirror is that tooling:
'   poll    host:list-forward every 150 ms
'   mirror  listen 127.0.0.1:<P> in the VM per tcp forward
'   carry   per connection: host:transport:<serial>, then the forward's own
'           target, through the adb server — no host port, no extra allow
'   drop    close the listener when the forward disappears; a taken port is
'           retried on the next poll
' MOBILEMCP_LEGACY_ROBOT=1 would skip mobilecli (plain adb shell), but its
' element list runs `uiautomator dump /dev/tty`, which API 36 kills (on the
' host as well), so legacy mode loses the accessibility tree.
'
' ── MEASURED (e2e, rebuilt image, 2026-09-30) ──────────────────────────────
'   install          mobile-mcp 1.0.6 via npm, ~5 s, 133 MB
'   tools            list devices, launch app, element list (@e1…), tap,
'                    screenshot (text + image), HOME: all error=False
'   host server      same pid before and after every guest session
'   telemetry        posthog + scarf only in runs without the opt-out
'   choice form      android ticked by keystroke (Down, Right, Space, Enter)
'                    in `proveo run claudecode --shell`: the run boots the
'                    AVD, the sandbox reads PROVEO_HOST_ADB_PORT=5037 and
'                    its adb lists emulator-5554; left unticked, no device
'                    appears, no "android:" line, the env stays unset
'
' ── AN ANDROID APP IN THE WORKSPACE (e2e/testdata/android-hello) ───────────
' A stock Gradle project: AGP 9.4.1, compileSdk/targetSdk 36, one Activity,
' no dependencies, no mise.toml. install.sh runs `gradle assembleDebug`, then
' `adb install -r` through ADB_SERVER_SOCKET.
' The seed provisions it from the sources alone (ensure_jvm_toolchain, a row of
' ensure_project_tools), inside the sandbox only:
'   detect   build.gradle[.kts] / settings.gradle[.kts] → gradle;
'            a com.android.* plugin in them → android
'   java     the image's JDK when ≥ 17, else mise java@temurin-21
'   gradle   nothing when ./gradlew exists, else mise gradle@latest
'   android  mise android-sdk@20.0, licenses accepted, ANDROID_HOME persisted;
'            AGP fetches platform + build-tools itself
' Google ships aapt2, aidl and zipalign for x86_64 Linux only (issuetracker
' 227219818; no linux-aarch64 archive in repository2-3.xml), and a sandbox
' takes the host CPU's architecture. cmdline-tools 23.0's sdkmanager also
' forwards to an x86_64-only `android` binary, hence 20.0.
'   amd64 guest                native, nothing extra
'   arm64 guest, macOS host    PROVEO_HOST_OS=darwin: build-tools 36.0.0 too,
'                              and a marked ~/.gradle/gradle.properties block
'                              sets android.aapt2FromMavenOverride to
'                              /usr/local/lib/proveo/aapt2, which runs that
'                              x86_64 aapt2 under qemu-user (base image, arm64
'                              only: qemu-user + amd64-cross libc, ~13 MB)
'   arm64 guest, other host    notice, no SDK: no measured path
'
' ── TOOLS PROVISIONED AFTER LAUNCH REACH THE AGENT ─────────────────────────
' sbx starts the agent before the seed provisions, and Claude Code snapshots
' its shell at start, so `!./install.sh` read `gradle: command not found`
' (opencode re-reads its shell and was fine). Claude Code re-sources
' CLAUDE_ENV_FILE before each Bash command, but only a hook may write it:
'   seed     _proveo_persist_tool_env writes ~/.proveo-tool-env.sh beside the
'            ~/.bashrc block
'   hook     proveo_install_claude_env_hook adds one SessionStart hook that
'            appends `[ -f ~/.proveo-tool-env.sh ] && . ~/.proveo-tool-env.sh`
'            to CLAUDE_ENV_FILE; installed before proveo_release_agent, which
'            the claude shim waits on
' Measured: an operator-set CLAUDE_ENV_FILE is ignored; a FileChanged hook
' sees files in the session cwd only; the SessionStart line picks up a file
' written after launch on the next command.
' respondToBashCommands defaults to false (seeded only when unset), so a `!`
' line costs no model call.
'
' ── CLAUDE CODE ON A LOCAL MODEL ───────────────────────────────────────────
' Each turn sends ~15k prompt tokens; side requests on the same single-slot
' Ollama model evicted the cached prompt, the 3-6 min reprocess outlasted the
' first-byte wait, and Claude Code retried forever. localModelArgs adds:
'   CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=low, CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_THINKING=1
'   CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1
'   API_TIMEOUT_MS, CLAUDE_STREAM_FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT_MS = 20 min
' and claude gets `--tools Bash,Read,Edit,Write` (withLocalModelTools; the
' entrypoint's CLAUDE_LOCAL_ARGS on docker). Trivial prompt on glimmer:
' default 495 s, trimmed 245 s, hooks and CLAUDE.md kept. CLAUDE_CODE_SIMPLE
' was 90 s but drops hooks and CLAUDE.md, so it is not used.
'
' ── THE USER-STYLE E2E (e2e/android_app_test.go) ───────────────────────────
' One subtest per harness row (opencode, claudecode), local model
' muse-glimmer:30b-mlx, no hosted inference:
'   form       `proveo run <h>` → [x] android by keystroke → Enter
'   sandbox    reaches the host emulator; the seed log shows the Android build
'   TUI        first-run dialogs answered as a user would; `!./install.sh`
'   host       pm list packages ca.proveo.hello; am start -W → Status: ok
'   agent      typed prompt; MOBILE-CHECK hello=yes, absent=no; a mobile
'              tool INVOCATION in the harness's own session record
'
' ── WHAT THE AGENT CAN DO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' ADB is full control of every device on that server. The server also dials:
' host:connect opens a TCP socket FROM THE HOST, outside sbx egress, and the
' emulator's own traffic leaves through the host's network. The run warns so.
' A relay that forwards only device services is the deferred fix
' (mobile-device-reach.puml).
' [Unverified] whether sbx enforces the Kit allow on the direct path; the
' host's global policy was allow-all during every measurement.

actor "Operator" as OP
node "host" as HOST {
  component "proveo run" as RUN
  component "adb server\n127.0.0.1:5037" as ADB
  component "Android emulator\nwindowed AVD" as EMU
}
node "sbx microVM" as VM {
  component "claude (sbx agent)\n--mcp-config, injected host-side" as AG
  component "mobile-mcp\nADB_SERVER_SOCKET=tcp:host.docker.internal:5037" as MCP
  component "adb-mirror\n127.0.0.1:<P> per forward" as MIR
}

OP --> EMU : watches, logs in once
RUN --> ADB : start-server
RUN --> EMU : reuse or boot
RUN --> VM : Kit allow localhost:5037\nenv PROVEO_HOST_ADB_PORT
AG --> MCP : stdio MCP
MCP --> ADB : adb protocol by IP
MCP --> MIR : http://localhost:<P>
MIR --> ADB : transport + forward target
ADB --> EMU : emulator-5554

note right of ADB
  **The server is the seam.** A fresh VM key
  reads unauthorized on adbd :5555; the server
  holds the host key and answers the VM, so
  the key never leaves the host.
end note

note right of MCP
  **The harness thinks, mobile-mcp acts.** Its
  tools are primitives: tap, swipe, type, the
  element list, a screenshot. No model runs
  inside it, so no second key is needed.
end note

note right of MIR
  **A forward, carried by number.** The host
  listener sits on the host's loopback; the
  mirror opens the same device socket through
  the server, so no extra port is allowed.
end note
@enduml
